<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Shamash-shum-ukin</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. 668–648 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century-bce">7th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Shamash-shum-ukin was king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/babylon">Babylon</a> from 668 to 648 BCE, a son of the Assyrian king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/esarhaddon">Esarhaddon</a>, who made him ruler of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/babylonia">Babylonia</a> under his younger brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ashurbanipal">Ashurbanipal</a>. In 652 BCE he rebelled with the support of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chaldean-empire">Chaldeans</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elamites">Elamites</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabs">Arabs</a>. Ashurbanipal besieged Babylon, and Shamash-shum-ukin died when the city fell in 648 BCE.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/shamash-shum-ukin.jpg" alt="Shamash-shum-ukin" width="320" height="306" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Zunkir · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Seal_of_Shamash-shum-ukin_BM_77611.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
